                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>Secretary of State Dulles departed from Washington on the evening of April 20 for
                    Paris to meet with British and French officials regarding Indochina and the
                    impending Geneva Conference. The Secretary also participated in a one-day
                    meeting of the North Atlantic Council on April 23. He departed Paris for Geneva
                    on the evening of April 24 at 9:20 p.m. (Paris time).</p>
                <p>Before the Secretary’s departure from Washington, he issued a statement regarding
                    the Geneva Conference (Department of State press release 207, April 20); for
                    text, see the Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, May 3,
                    1954, page 669.</p>
            </div>
